#### 2.3.1 Dual currency deposit/loan

A dual currency deposit (DCD) is a very popular and liquidly traded standard FX-linked investment, that works like a _reverse convertible bond_ in the equity markets. Investors searching for higher yields are selling a vanilla call on the deposit currency, which is also a put on another currency, to receive a higher coupon and then hope that the option they sold will be out-of-the-money at maturity. Some banks also name it _enhanced deposit_.

